   "role": "assistant",
   "content": "The rounding logic is in the `line_amount` function. It uses Python's built-in `round` function, which performs banker's rounding.  This means that when a number is halfway between two values, it rounds to the nearest even number.  \n\nTo fix this, we need to use the `quantize` method of the `Decimal` object with the `ROUND_HALF_UP` rounding mode. This will ensure that the amount is always rounded up to the nearest cent.\n\n```tool\n{\"tool\": \"edit_file\", \"args\": {\"path\": \"report.py\", \"find\": \"return round(amt, 2)\", \"replace\": \"return Decimal(str(amt)).quantize(Decimal('0.01'), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)\"}\n``` \n\n\n\n",
